From: XR1710G Community <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 11:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: report only terminal tx failures

cfg80211 defines tx_failed as transmissions that exhausted their retries
without receiving an ACK.  MT7996 TX-Free-Done provides the retry count in
MT_TXFREE_INFO_COUNT and the terminal outcome in MT_TXFREE_INFO_STAT.

The driver currently adds the retry count to both tx_retries and tx_failed.
As a result, a successfully delivered MPDU that needed retries is also
reported as failed, and `iw station dump` commonly shows tx_failed almost
equal to tx_retries even when packet delivery is healthy.

Count retries only in tx_retries and use the terminal status bit for
tx_failed.  This matches the cfg80211 ABI and the mt7925 TX-Free-Done path.

Signed-off-by: XR1710G Community <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 mt7996/mac.c | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mt7996/mac.c b/mt7996/mac.c
index 367b51a..c7e208f 100644
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -1362,7 +1362,7 @@ next:
 				cur_info++;
 			continue;
 		} else if (info & MT_TXFREE_INFO_HEADER) {
-			u32 tx_retries = 0, tx_failed = 0, count;
+			u32 tx_retries = 0, count;
 
 			if (!wcid)
 				continue;
@@ -1370,11 +1370,10 @@ next:
 
 			count = FIELD_GET(MT_TXFREE_INFO_COUNT, info);
 			tx_retries = count ? count - 1 : 0;
-			tx_failed = tx_retries +
-				!!FIELD_GET(MT_TXFREE_INFO_STAT, info);
 
 			wcid->stats.tx_retries += tx_retries;
-			wcid->stats.tx_failed += tx_failed;
+			wcid->stats.tx_failed +=
+				!!FIELD_GET(MT_TXFREE_INFO_STAT, info);
 			continue;
 		}
 
